💭 A cast that fails, handed straight to a call instead of being bound to a variable.
💭
💭 Expected: the program prints "it is no balloon" three times and then "still here: stone".
💭 What happens: see README.md. ASTCast::downcast releases the value in the branch where
💭 the cast fails, on the assumption that it was retained, which is so only when the cast
💭 is bound. Handed straight to a call, the object is read without a retain and then
💭 released, once for each failing cast.
💭
💭 Binding the cast is fine: ↪️ 🔲 thing 🎈 ➡️ balloon 🍇 … 🍉.
